      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, quick sanity check on something. i was looking at the latest merge for the validator selection logic in the protocol's core repo. there's this weirdly specific implementation of the LFSR (linear feedback shift register) parameters that looks almost identical to the one i used in my private alpha builds before the foundation scrubbed my access. \n\nthe way the polynomial coefficients are mapped to the state transitions—it's such a niche, weird way to handle it, but it's exactly how i optimized it to avoid the collision issues back then. can you verify if that specific coefficient mapping is actually in the current production build? i need to know if they're still running my exact (uncredited) logic under their own names or if they actually managed to refactor it.",
